---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import MyPicture from "@/assets/images/my-picture.jpg";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import CurrentPlayer from "@/components/currentPlayer.svelte";
---

<Layout title="Yogesh S">
	<main class="p-5 flex flex-col gap-5 font-urbanist text-lg">
		<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center gap-10">
			<Image
				height={150}
				width={150}
				class="rounded-full"
				src={MyPicture}
				quality="high"
				loading="eager"
				alt="Myself"
			/>
			<h1 class="font-bold text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-urbanist-italic">
				Hi! I'm Yogesh
			</h1>
		</div>
		<div>
			<p class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert">
				Hey, I'm Yogesh.

				I enjoy building ambitious software products-from AI-powered web applications and developer platforms to cross-platform desktop experiences.

				My work sits at the intersection of product engineering, frontend architecture, and developer experience. I care deeply about building systems that are fast, maintainable, and enjoyable to use, both for customers and the engineers who work on them.

				Over the years I've helped build and scale products used by thousands of users, architected frontend platforms from the ground up, and shipped features across the entire stack when needed.

				I like solving difficult engineering problems, simplifying complex user experiences, and turning ideas into products people actually use.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h2 class="font-bold cursor-default text-4xl text-red-300 w-fit">
				About Me
			</h2>
			<p>
				My journey into software started in an unexpected place.

				I graduated in 2021 with a degree in Electrical and Electronics Engineering from SRM Valliammai Engineering College. While I enjoyed understanding how hardware systems worked, I found myself increasingly drawn toward software-the speed of iteration, the creativity involved in building things, and the ability to bring ideas to life with nothing more than a laptop and curiosity.

				What began with learning HTML, CSS, and JavaScript quickly turned into a full-time obsession. I spent countless hours exploring modern web technologies, breaking things, fixing them, and gradually developing a deeper appreciation for software engineering as a craft.

				Today, I enjoy building products that sit at the intersection of usability, performance, and maintainability. Whether it's architecting large frontend systems, designing developer tooling, building real-time experiences, or working across the stack to solve product problems, I'm most motivated when I'm turning complexity into something simple and reliable.

				Over the years, I've worked on AI-powered applications, document-processing systems, cross-platform desktop software, developer platforms, and collaborative workflows. Regardless of the problem space, I care deeply about creating software that feels fast, intuitive, and dependable.

				Outside of work, I enjoy exploring new technologies, studying how successful products are built, and experimenting with side projects that help me learn something new.
			</p>
		</div>
		<CurrentPlayer client:load />
	</main>
</Layout>
